# Glasspool Mimic copies "a creature you control" (CR 614.1c): Bot2's Ornithopter (0/2) was on the battlefield first, then Bot1's Memnite
# (1/1). Only the Memnite is a creature Bot1 controls, so the Mimic enters as a copy of it without a choice (one candidate): a 1/1
# Construct Shapeshifter Rogue. An engine that also offered the opponent's creature would ask which, and the Ornithopter, first
# on the battlefield, would be the one it copies.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Memnite
Glasspool Mimic
Island x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x19

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Glasspool Mimic.Cast
Bot1.Accept
[T5 Bot1.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Memnite; Memnite
Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite#2.Subtypes = Construct; Rogue; Shapeshifter
Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite#2.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite#2.Toughness = 1
Bot2.Battlefield = Ornithopter
